<Layout title="Context">
	<h1>Context</h1>
	
	<p>As automated systems manage increasingly complex tasks, authority often becomes implicit—embedded in code, configurations, or operational assumptions rather than explicitly declared. This creates a governance gap where it is unclear who or what is authorized to make a specific decision.</p>

	<p>Audit logs and explainability tools address what happened and why, but they do not establish whether the action was authorized in the first place. Authorization requires a prospective declaration of authority, distinct from retrospective analysis.</p>

	<p>DAL exists to address this structural class of governance problem by formalizing decision authority as a distinct concern.</p>

	<p style="margin-top: 2rem;">
		<a href="https://blockchaination.github.io/decision-authority-layer/spec/">Read the DAL Specification &rarr;</a>
	</p>
